>
  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="why">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Why service your boiler every year?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A yearly service keeps your boiler safe, keeps the warranty valid and finds small faults before they turn into a winter breakdown.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Safety.</strong> A faulty boiler can leak carbon monoxide. You cannot see it or smell it. A service checks the boiler burns gas safely and the flue takes fumes outside.</li>
        <li><strong>Warranty.</strong> Most boiler makers ask for a service every 12 months. Without it, they can refuse a claim.</li>
        <li><strong>Fewer breakdowns.</strong> We spot worn parts early. A part changed in summer is cheaper and easier than a breakdown in January.</li>
        <li><strong>Lower running costs.</strong> A clean, well set-up boiler uses gas better than a neglected one.</li>
        <li><strong>A longer life.</strong> Most gas boilers last 10 to 15 years. One that is serviced every year usually lasts longer.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/domestic/" rel="noopener">Health and Safety Executive</a> advises that gas appliances are serviced every year. Read our <a href="/blog/carbon-monoxide-safety-liverpool">carbon monoxide safety guide</a> for the warning signs.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="checks">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What does a boiler service include?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">We take the cover off, clean and check the parts inside, and test that the boiler burns gas safely. Here is the full list.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Safety checks</h3>
          <ul class="sg-ticks">
            <li>Flue gas analysis, to prove the boiler burns gas cleanly</li>
            <li>Gas pressure and gas rate checked</li>
            <li>The flue checked along its route, with seals and joints</li>
            <li>Safety devices tested, so the boiler shuts down if it should</li>
            <li>Air supply and ventilation checked</li>
            <li>Your carbon monoxide alarm tested, if you have one</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Inside the boiler</h3>
          <ul class="sg-ticks">
            <li>Burner and heat exchanger checked and cleaned</li>
            <li>Condensate trap cleaned, and the condensate pipe checked</li>
            <li>Seals and gaskets checked for wear</li>
            <li>System pressure and expansion vessel checked</li>
            <li>Inhibitor level checked and topped up if low</li>
            <li>Magnetic filter cleaned, if you have one</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3>To finish</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>Heating and hot water run and tested, with the controls and thermostat.</li>
        <li>The Benchmark service record filled in.</li>
        <li>A copy of the service record emailed to you the same day.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How does the visit work?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">You book a time, we service the boiler in about an hour, and you get the record by email the same day.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Book (2 minutes).</strong> Call or <a href="/get-started">book online</a>. Tell us the make of boiler if you know it. The price is fixed at £120.</li>
        <li><strong>We arrive.</strong> A Gas Safe registered engineer comes at the agreed time. Anyone can let us in. You can ask to see the Gas Safe card.</li>
        <li><strong>The service (45 to 60 minutes).</strong> We work through the full checklist above. We use dust sheets and tidy up after.</li>
        <li><strong>What we found.</strong> We tell you how the boiler is doing. If something needs fixing, you get a price first. You decide.</li>
        <li><strong>Your record.</strong> We fill in the Benchmark record and email you a copy the same day.</li>
        <li><strong>Next year.</strong> We send a free reminder when the next service is due.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Boiler due a service?</strong> Call and we will find you the next free slot.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="which">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which option is right for me?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Most home owners need the £120 boiler service. Landlords should book the £199 service and gas safety certificate. Add the £120 cylinder service if you have an unvented hot water cylinder.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>You own your home</h3>
          <p>Book the <strong>boiler service for £120</strong>. It keeps the warranty valid and the boiler safe. You do not need a gas safety certificate by law.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>You rent out a home</h3>
          <p>Book the <strong>service and certificate for £199</strong>. You need the gas safety certificate every 12 months by law. Doing both in one visit saves you £20 and one trip for your tenant.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3>Do you have a cylinder as well as a boiler?</h3>
      <p>If your hot water comes from a mains pressure (unvented) cylinder, it needs its own yearly service too. Cylinder makers ask for it to keep the warranty. Ours is £120, and all our engineers are G3 qualified for unvented cylinders. See our <a href="/hot-water-cylinders-liverpool">hot water cylinders</a> page for more.</p>
      <p>A combi boiler has no cylinder, so you only need the boiler service.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="vs-cp12">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Boiler service or gas safety certificate?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">They are two different jobs. A service looks after the boiler. A gas safety certificate proves every gas appliance is safe, and landlords need one by law.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th></th><th>Boiler service</th><th>Gas safety certificate (CP12)</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>What it does</strong></td><td>Cleans, tests and sets up the boiler inside</td><td>Checks every gas appliance is safe to use</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Covers</strong></td><td>The boiler</td><td>Boiler, gas cooker and hob</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Needed by law?</strong></td><td>No, but most warranties need it</td><td>Yes, for landlords, every 12 months</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Paperwork</strong></td><td>Benchmark service record</td><td>Landlord gas safety record</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Price</strong></td><td>£120</td><td>£100</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Both in one visit cost <strong>£199</strong>. See our <a href="/gas-safety-certificate-liverpool">gas safety certificate</a> page for what landlords must do.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="warranty">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Will a service keep my boiler warranty valid?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Most boiler makers want a service every 12 months by a Gas Safe registered engineer, written in the Benchmark record. We do both on every visit.</p>
      <p>Your boiler came with a Benchmark checklist. It is usually in the back of the manual, or kept online. Each service goes into it. If the boiler breaks down under warranty, the maker can ask to see it.</p>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Tip:</strong> keep the service date close to the date the boiler was fitted. Some makers ask for the service within 12 months of the last one. Our reminder helps you stay on time.</p></div>
      <p>Warranty lengths depend on the boiler. For example, the Baxi 800 we fit comes with 10 years of cover. See our <a href="/boiler-installation-liverpool">new boiler packages</a> for each one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="signs">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Does your boiler need a check now?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">If you see any of these signs, do not wait for the yearly service. Call us and we will take a look.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>The boiler keeps locking out or showing an error code.</li>
        <li>The pressure keeps dropping, and you keep topping it up.</li>
        <li>Banging, gurgling or whistling noises.</li>
        <li>Heating but no hot water, or hot water but no heating.</li>
        <li>Black marks or soot around the boiler.</li>
        <li>It has been more than 12 months since the last service.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="brx-danger"><p><strong>Yellow or orange flame, or a carbon monoxide alarm going off?</strong> Turn the boiler off if you can, open the windows and get everyone outside. Call the National Gas Emergency Service on <a href="tel:0800111999">0800 111 999</a> first. Then ring us to find the fault.</p></div>
      <p>If the boiler has stopped working, you need a repair, not a service. See <a href="/boiler-repair-liverpool">boiler repair</a>. If radiators are cold at the bottom, sludge may be the cause, and a <a href="/power-flushing-liverpool">power flush</a> can help.</p>
      <h3>Is my boiler too old to service?</h3>
      <p>Most boilers can still be serviced at any age. After 10 to 15 years, parts get harder to find. If yours keeps breaking down, we will tell you honestly if a <a href="/boiler-installation-liverpool">new boiler</a> makes more sense. Planning a bigger job? See <a href="/central-heating-installation-liverpool">central heating installation</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
